# 11. Comparison Operators

Comparison operators compare two values.

They return a Boolean:

```text
true
false
```

Common comparison operators:

| Operator | Meaning                         |
| -------- | ------------------------------- |
| `==`     | Equal after type conversion     |
| `===`    | Strictly equal                  |
| `!=`     | Not equal after type conversion |
| `!==`    | Strictly not equal              |
| `>`      | Greater than                    |
| `<`      | Less than                       |
| `>=`     | Greater than or equal           |
| `<=`     | Less than or equal              |

---

# 12. Equal `==`

The `==` operator compares values after allowing type conversion.

```javascript
console.log(5 == "5");
```

Output:

```text
true
```

The number `5` and string `"5"` are converted for the comparison.

---

# 13. Strict Equal `===`

The `===` operator checks both value and type.

```javascript
console.log(5 === "5");
```

Output:

```text
false
```

Because:

```text
5   → number
"5" → string
```

Example:

```javascript
console.log(5 === 5);
```

Output:

```text
true
```

For modern JavaScript, `===` is generally preferred when you want predictable equality checks.

---

# 14. Not Equal `!=`

```javascript
console.log(5 != 10);
```

Output:

```text
true
```

Because `5` is not equal to `10`.

---

# 15. Strict Not Equal `!==`

```javascript
console.log(5 !== "5");
```

Output:

```text
true
```

The values have different types.

---

# 16. Greater Than `>`

```javascript
console.log(10 > 5);
```

Output:

```text
true
```

---

# 17. Less Than `<`

```javascript
console.log(10 < 5);
```

Output:

```text
false
```

---

# 18. Greater Than or Equal `>=`

```javascript
console.log(10 >= 10);
```

Output:

```text
true
```

---

# 19. Less Than or Equal `<=`

```javascript
console.log(10 <= 10);
```

Output:

```text
true
```

---

# 20. Comparison Example

```javascript
let age = 22;

console.log(age > 18);
console.log(age < 18);
console.log(age === 22);
console.log(age !== 30);
```

Output:

```text
true
false
true
true
```

