# 42. Bitwise Operators

Bitwise operators work with the bit-level representation of numbers.

Common operators:

| Operator | Name                         |    |
| -------- | ---------------------------- | -- |
| `&`      | AND                          |    |
| `        | `                            | OR |
| `^`      | XOR                          |    |
| `~`      | NOT                          |    |
| `<<`     | Left shift                   |    |
| `>>`     | Sign-propagating right shift |    |
| `>>>`    | Zero-fill right shift        |    |

Example:

```javascript
console.log(5 & 1);
```

Output:

```text
1
```

Binary representation:

```text
5 = 101
1 = 001

101
001
---
001 = 1
```

Bitwise operators are more common in specialized programming such as low-level operations, flags, binary manipulation, and some performance-sensitive algorithms.

