# 50. Logical Operators in Real Applications

Example from an authentication system:

```javascript
const isLoggedIn = true;
const isAdmin = true;

if (isLoggedIn && isAdmin) {
    console.log("Access granted");
}
```

Output:

```text
Access granted
```

Another example:

```javascript
const role = "admin";

if (role === "admin" || role === "manager") {
    console.log("Can access dashboard");
}
```

---

# 51. Operator Example in a Hotel System

```javascript
const capacity = 6;
const customerCount = 4;

const availableSeats = capacity - customerCount;

console.log(availableSeats);
```

Output:

```text
2
```

Check availability:

```javascript
if (customerCount < capacity) {
    console.log("Table available");
} else {
    console.log("Table full");
}
```

